            "text": "Renewable energy can significantly reduce greenhouse gas emissions and improve public health.",
            "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
            "id": "1",
            "text": "Iceland and Denmark are leading countries in renewable energy usage.",
            "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
            "id": "2",
            "text": "Costa Rica generates over 95% of its power from renewable sources.",
            "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
            "id": "3",
            "text": "International Renewable Energy Agency (IRENA) reports that it is technically and economically feasible to transition to 90% renewable energy by 2050.",
            "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
            "id": "4",
            "text": "Public support and awareness are important for a full transition to renewable energy.",
            "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
            "id": "5",
            "text": "Transition to 100% renewable energy is technically possible but requires significant investment, policy changes, and public support.",
            "event": "ADD"
        }
    ]
}

